{%- comment -%}
  THE BUILD YOUR TEAM STORE PAGE IS RENDERED FROM THE THEME, NOT FROM
  ITS PAGE BODY, AND IT IS KEYED ON THE HANDLE ON PURPOSE.

  The conventional way to give one page its own markup is a template
  suffix, templates/page.build-your-store.json, selected on the page
  record in admin. That is deliberately NOT used here, because the
  template suffix is a property of the PAGE, which is global: setting it
  would make every theme look for that template, including the live one,
  which does not have it. The page would break on live the moment the
  suffix was set, before this theme was ever published.

  A handle check inside main-page keeps the whole change inside the
  theme. Nothing about the page record changes, live keeps rendering the
  page body exactly as before, and this theme renders the builder from
  snippets/team-store-builder.liquid instead. Preview shows the new one,
  live shows the old one, and publishing is what swaps them.

  It also survives publishing, so it is not a temporary hack: once this
  theme is live, page.content is simply no longer the source.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if page.handle == 'build-your-store' -%}

  {{ 'trh-builder.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {%- comment -%}
    The brighter layer and the animated header, 2026-11-11. The layer must
    load AFTER trh-builder.css. The header sits outside page-width so it can
    run full bleed, and tbh-page wraps both so the header can shrink once
    the builder is past step 1 (it reads the builder's own step rail).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {{ 'trh-builder-pop.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <div class="tbh-page">
  {%- render 'trh-builder-hero' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Full bleed rather than page-width--narrow, and outside .rte. The
    narrow column is right for prose and wrong for a product grid, and
    .rte restyles headings, lists and tables underneath the builder's
    own rules.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="page-width">
    {%- render 'team-store-builder' -%}
  </div>
  </div>

{%- else -%}

  <div class="page-width page-width--narrow page-content">
    {%- render 'breadcrumbs' -%}
    <header class="section-header">
      <h1 class="section-header__title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="rte rte--nomargin">
      {{ page.content }}
    </div>
  </div>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.main-page.name",
  "tag": "section"
}
{% endschema %}
